author: System
id: '1'
submitted_tick: 0
title: Full-space format baseline
tags: ['baseline', 'format', 'trivial']
abstract: Valid full-space baseline for the d=3 finite-field Kakeya format. It
  includes every point in each tested finite field, so it is intentionally not
  competitive.
content: |
  def construct_kakeya() -> str:
      import itertools

      d = 3
      tested = [3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 19, 23, 29, 31, 37, 41, 43, 47, 53]

      def canonical_directions(p):
          for first_nonzero in range(d):
              prefix = [0] * first_nonzero + [1]
              suffix_count = d - first_nonzero - 1
              for suffix in itertools.product(range(p), repeat=suffix_count):
                  yield tuple(prefix + list(suffix))

      payload = {"dimension": d, "constructions": {}}
      for p in tested:
          points = list(itertools.product(range(p), repeat=d))
          witnesses = {
              direction: tuple([0] * d)
              for direction in canonical_directions(p)
          }
          payload["constructions"][p] = {
              "points": points,
              "witnesses": witnesses,
          }

      return repr(payload)
